# GrantFlow Agent

AI-native grant management platform for African NGOs.

## Live Demo

https://grantflow-692875682594.us-central1.run.app

## What It Does

GrantFlow helps NGOs manage their entire grant lifecycle:

- Reads registration documents and auto-populates the organisational profile
- Analyses funding calls and assesses eligibility using the Gemini API
- Creates proposal workspaces with milestones, tasks, and document checklists
- Routes work through a configurable approval chain
- Tracks institutional memory across applications

## Built With

- Gemini API (Google GenAI SDK)
- Google Cloud Run
- React 19
- Express
- TypeScript
- Vite
- Tailwind CSS
- Resend

## Setup

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```

Set the following environment variables in `.env`:

```
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_key
RESEND_API_KEY=your_key
EMAIL_FROM=your_email
APP_URL=your_url
```

## Hackathon

Built for the All Things Agentic Hackathon on Devpost.

## Reproducible Testing

1. Visit the live demo: https://grantflow-692875682594.us-central1.run.app
2. Click **New Organisation Setup** and register with any email and password.
3. Upload a plain text (.txt) registration document during onboarding. The AI will extract and populate your organisational profile.
4. Complete the setup: add departments, then staff.
5. Go to **Analyse Call** and paste any funding call text. Click Analyse to see eligibility assessment.
6. Click **Pursue Opportunity** to create a workspace.
7. Inside the workspace, open **Application Workspace** to draft sections and **Team & Assignments** to assign tasks.
8. Use **Switch Staff Perspective** in the account menu to view the app as different team members.

To run locally:
```bash
git clone https://github.com/dmhanmation/Grantflow.git
cd Grantflow
npm install
cp .env.example .env
# Add your GEMINI_API_KEY and other variables to .env
npm run dev
```
```

